    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Dostoevsky returns for his adult preventive visit two weeks after his eight-month review. He has had no seizure since the breakthrough seizure during his trip and has taken every lamotrigine dose, using his phone alarms. He has not gambled since returning home; he resumed weekly cognitive behavioral therapy, attends a Gamblers Anonymous meeting each week, and has set up a repayment plan with a nonprofit debt counselor. He is sleeping about seven hours a night and has stopped writing through the night. His mood has lifted since the last visit. He completed the health risk assessment before the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Adult preventive visit, age 43</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Epilepsy of unknown type on lamotrigine; gambling disorder in early recovery after a lapse</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Lamotrigine 100 mg twice daily</td></tr><tr><td>Since the last visit</td><td>No seizure, no gambling, every dose taken</td></tr><tr><td>Functional status</td><td>Independent; writing to his usual schedule</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Fair, and improving</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Debts under a repayment plan; close friends; weekly therapy and peer support; lives alone</td></tr><tr><td>Behavioral</td><td>Never smoker; alcohol one or two glasses of wine a week (AUDIT-C 2); no other drug use; walks daily</td></tr><tr><td>Gambling</td><td>No gambling for five weeks, since he came home; self-exclusion and bank gambling block active</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent in all</td></tr><tr><td>Instrumental activities of daily living</td><td>Manages his own medicines with a pill organizer and alarms; a friend he trusts co-signs any withdrawal over a set amount</td></tr><tr><td>Home safety</td><td>Smoke detector working; showers rather than baths; no firearms</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About seven hours a night since he stopped writing through the night</td></tr><tr><td>Driving</td><td>Not driving</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>No concerns; reading glasses</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

