    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given. Depression screen negative (PHQ-2 1). AUDIT-C 2. Ten-year cardiovascular risk under 5 percent from his intake lipids and today&apos;s blood pressure. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Epilepsy on lamotrigine (G40.909)</content>. No seizure since the provoked breakthrough seizure; adherence restored. [S]<list><item>Continue lamotrigine 100 mg twice daily.</item><item>Neurology review in January, as planned.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Gambling disorder, early recovery after a lapse (F63.0)</content>. No gambling since the lapse; therapy, peer support, and debt counseling in place. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide; the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline and the problem-gambling helpline are in his phone. [S]<list><item>Continue weekly cognitive behavioral therapy and Gamblers Anonymous.</item><item>Chronic-care review in three months.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, 1865-1866</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Inactivated vaccine given today</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, 1865-1866</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended; he will get it at his pharmacy</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Universal adult vaccination through age 59; no prior doses on record. First of two HepB-CpG doses given today; second dose in one month</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis booster</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap about five and a half years ago; next due in about four and a half years</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C and HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time screening for adults; no prior result on record; drawn today with his consent</td></tr><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>122/78 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol and statin decision</td><td>Up to date</td><td>LDL 108 mg/dL at intake; ten-year risk under 5 percent, so a statin is not indicated; recheck in five years</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>HbA1c 5.3 percent at intake; BMI 23.6</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Due</td><td>Starts at 45; options discussed so that he can choose when he turns 45</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 1; PHQ-9 9 two weeks ago</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C 2; alcohol is also a seizure trigger, and he keeps to one or two glasses a week</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never smoker</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer and abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never smoker and under the starting ages</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Shared decision-making begins at 55</td></tr><tr><td>Bone health on antiseizure medicine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Vitamin D 32 ng/mL at intake; lamotrigine is not an enzyme inducer, so no DXA scan is needed</td></tr><tr><td>Eye examination</td><td>Due</td><td>No examination in more than two years; he will book with an optometrist</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, 1865-1866 season; Hepatitis B vaccine (HepB-CpG), dose 1 of 2 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Hepatitis C and HIV results by message. Second hepatitis B dose in one month at a nurse visit. Neurology review in January. Chronic-care review in three months. Next preventive visit in one year. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
